      "role": "user",
      "content": "but \"economic inefficiency\" is just a way of saying it's better for corporations to have cheap labor abroad than for local workers to have good jobs. isn't it kind of a biased way to look at it? like, shouldn't a country's main goal be the welfare of its own citizens rather than \"global cooperation\"?",
